This composition looks like a precipitation-hardened maraging stainless steel of the PH 13-8Mo type. That grade has about 12.5 Cr, 8 Ni, 2.2 Mo and 1.1 Al. The alloy here is close to it, with Cr 10.5, Ni 10.3, Mo 3.1, Al 0.36 and Ti 0.11. It looks like a Fe-Cr-Ni-Mo-Al-Ti maraging steel, so the Ni-Al and Ni-Ti precipitates should give strong hardening. I did not run any calculation or look up data. The figure below is a judgment from typical values for similar steels.

Such steels typically reach about 1400 MPa in the aged condition. The Al and Ti contents are low, so the precipitation hardening is modest. I therefore estimate roughly 1200 MPa.

